    description: "FOUND while fixing WI-gabuv (owner_ancestry, finalize sub-step 7d).\n\nSTATEMENT. A module whose `use X` injects X's functions WITHOUT declaring a behaviour has no relationship edge, so `owner_ancestry` cannot walk from the module to X and calls through the module stay `external_potential`. Verified from source for Tesla: `use Tesla` -> `use Tesla.Builder`, whose `__using__` quote registers attributes and splices `generate_http_verbs(opts)` (get/post/put/... and request) with no `@behaviour` (~/t5_stdlib_srcs/ex-tesla/lib/tesla/builder.ex:7-103). So `defmodule MyApi do use Tesla end` + `MyApi.get(\"/x\")` never reaches the shipped `Tesla` row in io_primitives_overlays/elixir-web-and-db.yaml. The elixir analyzer emits only a FILE-level `imports` edge (evidence `use_directive`) for such a `use`.\n\nRelated, same family: `use HTTPoison.Base` DOES declare `@behaviour HTTPoison.Base` (now in USE_IMPLIED_BEHAVIOURS, so the walk reaches `HTTPoison.Base`), but the `HTTPoison.Base` row lists only `request`/`request!` while `__using__` injects get/post/put/patch/delete/head/options and bang forms too (httpoison lib/httpoison/base.ex). Not measured on a corpus repository.\n\nFIX DIRECTION. Emit a module-level relationship for a `use` of a LIBRARY module whose __using__ is known to inject functions (a USE_INJECTS table beside USE_IMPLIED_BEHAVIOURS, read from source; `includes` is the closest existing edge type, which owner_ancestry already walks), rather than widening `implements` to mean something it does not. Then extend the HTTPoison.Base row to the injected verbs with a cited source."  # 324c
    fields: {}  # 324c
